   "score": 5,
   "text": "25 % 36 % 36 % He's averaging 11 and 1/2 shot attempts.",
   "me": 1,
   "child": 1
  },
  {
   "id": 94,
   "video": "KvBGTGbk0fw",
   "t": 523,
   "score": 4,
   "text": "I I I won like a ridiculous It was like 70% return on on NFL.",
   "me": 1,
   "child": 1
  },
  {
   "id": 98,
   "video": "YkOSnugS_k4",
   "t": 588,
   "score": 4,
   "text": "43% of his targets come in zones where the defense is favorable.",
   "me": 1,
   "child": 1
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "video": "jYoaIFeQklE",
   "t": 481,
   "score": 3,
   "text": "Every play is ranked from 60 to 100.",
   "me": 1,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "video": "Y-RsRjDpHVk",
   "t": 617,
   "score": 4,
   "text": "58.32% for that bet to hit.",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 1
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "video": "wb9qyIQKsYU",
   "t": 545,
   "score": 3,
   "text": "Now, when I bet this earlier, it was even more than 3650, but the thing that you need to realize and something that I am coming around to the idea",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "video": "8zKNNgz-uoc",
   "t": 537,
   "score": 7,
   "text": "Instead of just blindly betting every edge of 5% or more, you're more likely to increase your ROI and reduce your variance by applying a little critical thinking when choosing",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "video": "jDq9aRBXQTo",
   "t": 337,
   "score": 6,
   "text": "So you can start there and then you just go in, say, you know what, I really only want edge when it's 2%or more.",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "video": "KvBGTGbk0fw",
   "t": 1915,
   "score": 5,
   "text": "So, we don't want to be betting into 5% lines, but what we do have is the ability to take what traditional top-down plays would have, they would never be",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "video": "8zKNNgz-uoc",
   "t": 385,
   "score": 4,
   "text": "If Wagner would have been ruled out 30 minutes before the game and the lines moved on everyone else but one player who's still showing an edge 15 minutes later,",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 29,
   "video": "8zKNNgz-uoc",
   "t": 120,
   "score": 3,
   "text": "If you wanted to build a do-it-yourself solution, you would have to babysit dozens of beat writers and league sources every minute of the day.",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 37,
   "video": "9CrQ8f7tZQQ",
   "t": 792,
   "score": 3,
   "text": "this edge, it's going to win 350 units a week.\" And then you find out that there's a sign inversion.",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 39,
   "video": "8zKNNgz-uoc",
   "t": 521,
   "score": 4,
   "text": "The number one question I get asked all the time is, should I bet everything on the screen that shows an edge of 2 5 10 or whatever other percent?",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 42,
   "video": "jDq9aRBXQTo",
   "t": 264,
   "score": 7,
   "text": "So if I think it's, you know, 45%likely to occur, but it's actually 48%likely to occur, that's an edge of three.",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 47,
   "video": "K7p3d99XH6U",
   "t": 317,
   "score": 5,
   "text": "I don't want to play any of these plays that are below 2 and 1/2% so I'm going to take these three.",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 51,
   "video": "8zKNNgz-uoc",
   "t": 596,
   "score": 7,
   "text": "Is a 10% edge in a points prop the same as a 10% edge in a three-pointers made prop?",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 59,
   "video": "jDq9aRBXQTo",
   "t": 275,
   "score": 6,
   "text": "That's a 3%edge based on the pricing that the market is giving me.",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 61,
   "video": "jYoaIFeQklE",
   "t": 595,
   "score": 3,
   "text": "Meaning every time you get a play in that moves like that, you are gaining an edge towards the sports books or against the sports books.",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 75,
   "video": "KvBGTGbk0fw",
   "t": 2338,
   "score": 7,
   "text": "Um but anyway, so there's shit tons of things going in my head that I would choose down to 2% or -2% edge.",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 78,
   "video": "KvBGTGbk0fw",
   "t": 1809,
   "score": 4,
   "text": "So you get, um, 30% off your very first purchase at A Train Station.",
   "me": 0,
   "child": 0
  },
  {
   "id": 79,
   "video": "Cqo4AAeVeuI",
   "t": 329,
